 :motivation "Live production telemetry and Simon's browser chrome://webrtc-internals trace proved that synchronous 12MB Fressian validator snapshot serialization + writeFileSync on Node.js stalls the single-threaded event loop for 5-8s on e2-micro, starving Chrome's 5s WebRTC ICE STUN consent freshness probes (connected -> disconnected -> connected). Simultaneously, browser connect-webrtc! never wired pc.oniceconnectionstatechange / pc.onconnectionstatechange, leaving transient ICE flaps invisible in diagnostics (Rule 5 gap). Per Simon's architectural direction, BIP-014 eliminates synchronous disk/compression I/O on critical paths across ALL THREE runtimes (Node.js, JVM, Browser) and BOTH node roles (full node and light node), moving validator state persistence to immutable epoch-addressed async snapshots with tunable retention."
 :pillars
 [{:id "P-ASYNC-1"
   :name "Pure Sans-IO Immutable Epoch-Addressed Snapshot Core (src/bitecho/snapshot/core.cljc)"
   :summary "Pure, deterministic snapshot naming (snapshot-<node>-epoch-<012d>.fressian), highest-epoch recovery selection with seamless legacy fallback (snapshot-<node>.edn), tunable retention planner (keep-epochs default 360 ~= 1h at 10s/epoch, min-keep >= 2 always preserved), and single-authority generation-tagged coalescing async writer reducer (Rule 4 & Rule 5: at most 1 in-flight write + 1 latest pending epoch, stale-gen ignored & counted, failed writes never prune prior snapshots)."}
  {:id "P-ASYNC-2"
   :name "Node.js Zero-Sync-IO Full Node & Light Node (full_node_main.cljs, node_main.cljs)"
   :summary "Eliminate synchronous disk/compression I/O on all runtime critical paths (validator snapshots, blob GET/PUT, pointer snapshots, static content + gzip, telemetry digest GET/PUT, light-node state.fressian). Use fs.promises + async zlib + coalescing bitecho.snapshot.core writer, and offload/chunk heavy Fressian encoding so event-loop stall stays <= 50ms (eliminating Chrome 5s STUN consent-freshness drops). Boot-time config/identity load and SIGTERM final flush remain explicit exceptions."}
  {:id "P-ASYNC-3"
   :name "JVM Zero-Sync-IO Parity for Full Node & Light Node (shell/persistence.clj, shell/mesh.clj, shell/infra.clj, shell/light_node.clj)"
   :summary "Upgrade JVM full node persistence to the identical immutable epoch-addressed snapshot format + retention pruning via bitecho.snapshot.core on its dedicated persistence worker. Move JVM infra blob GET/PUT, pointer snapshots, telemetry digests, and light-node state.fressian saves off Netty/WebRTC/event-loop threads onto bounded async I/O executors with Rule 5 counted diagnostics."}
  {:id "P-ASYNC-4"
   :name "Browser WebRTC ICE & Connection-State Diagnostics (shell/browser.cljc, browser_main.cljs)"
   :summary "Wire pc.oniceconnectionstatechange and pc.onconnectionstatechange in connect-webrtc! to dispatch generation-tagged :ice-state-change and :connection-state-change events into transition-conn. Surface counted :ice-disconnects, :ice-reconnects, :last-ice-state, :last-connection-state, and counted :diagnose entries in getStatus().diagnostics (closing Rule 5 gap while preserving zero sync storage on browser hot paths)."}]
